REGEDIT4

; Use Microsoft's real d3dcompiler_47 instead of Wine's builtin.
;
; VirtualDJ compiles every "source only" visual at load time: 265 of the 720
; shaders in the library ship only shader.json (the ShaderToy source) with no
; compiled_D11_1.cso, and nothing caches the result -- not the .vdjshader (the
; files are untouched since the March download despite being played), not
; Cache/Plugins (store thumbnails only), not cache.db (waveforms only). So the
; compiler runs on every load and its output is what the GPU executes.
;
; It really is this DLL that serves those calls, though virtualdj.exe neither
; imports nor names it -- the name is built at runtime, so no string search
; finds it. Proved with WINEDEBUG=+loaddll (`vdj-bench probe`):
;   Loaded L"C:\\windows\\system32\\d3dcompiler_47.dll" ... : builtin
;
; Why it matters: source-only shaders measure a median 10.16x their catalog
; performance rating, against 3.90x for shaders that ship a prebuilt DXBC
; (n=277, measured 2026-09-12). Whether that gap is the compiler or simply
; curated-port-vs-auto-transpile is not settled -- this override is the
; experiment that answers it.
;
; "native,builtin" rather than plain "native" so a DLL that fails to load
; falls back instead of taking every visual down with it. Check which one
; actually won with `vdj-bench probe <id>`: the loaddll line says "builtin"
; or "native".
;
; To revert: drop this import and the install line from default.nix, rebuild,
; and delete the key below by hand (a .reg import never removes what an
; earlier one wrote -- same caution as fullscreen-monitor.reg).

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Wine\DllOverrides]
"d3dcompiler_47"="native,builtin"
